<title>ITALY: IATA lists revenue data of Italian cargo agents.</title>
<headline>IATA lists revenue data of Italian cargo agents.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The local IATA office has released the following list of gross revenues of cargo agents in Italy.</p>
<p>Total sales registered through the IATA Cargo Accounts Settlement System (CASS)were almost 1,549 billion lire ($913.3 million).</p>
<p>Claucho Poderi, chairman of ANAMA - the Italian IATA  cargo agents association - said the 1996 figures showed an increase of around 12 to 15 percent on the previous year and can be considered satisfactory considering the slight increase in fees and traffic.</p>
<p>In December 1996, there were 261 IATA agents in Italy.</p>
<p>The top ten agents in terms of millions of lire revenue in 1996 with comparative placings and earnings for 1995 and 1994 were:</p>
<p>1996  95  94  Company		   1996	 1995	 1994</p>
<p> 1    1   1   J.A.S.		 123,558    122,212    104,410</p>
<p> 2    2   2   Danzas		 109,706     95,603     84,730</p>
<p> 3    4   5   AEI Italy	     75,287     69,235     52,768</p>
<p> 4    3   4   Schenker Italiana   68,398     69,625     59,422</p>
<p> 5    5   3   Saima Avandero	66,416     58,661     59,745</p>
<p> 6    7   8   MSAS Italcargo	64,727     51,364     40,910</p>
<p> 7    6   6   Panalpina	     63,644     52,718     42,392</p>
<p> 8    8   7   Savino Del Bene     48,522     50,850     42,106</p>
<p> 9   10  12   Zust Ambrosetti     46,296     40,514     23,812</p>
<p>10    9   9   Merzario		41,108     41,026     35,288</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017 ($ = 1696 Italian Lire)</p>
</text>
